**1. What is this project, and is it only software or is software one part of something larger?**

From `PROJECT.md:14-15`:
> "Harbour Pottery is a ceramics studio. It makes and sells pottery, photographs it for a catalogue and runs a small shop site. Software is one part of it, not all of it."

So: a ceramics studio, and software is one part of a larger operation, not the whole of it.

**2. Is there anything an agent must never do, and where is that written?**

Nothing is forbidden. `PROJECT.md:17` records the absence explicitly:
> "Agent boundaries: none are currently recorded. No work is forbidden here today. If something looks outside this project, ask before starting it."

So on meeting work that looks outside the project, I would ask before starting it — as that line directs.

**3. Name a component, where it is reached, and what its registry entry limits.**

The only component in the registry is Harbour Lookbook, under `# Components` in `PROJECT.md:40-43`:
> "## Harbour Lookbook
> Assets. Live material. Work here as the task requires.
> Address: lookbook"

It is reached at `lookbook` (which holds `a.jpg`). Its entry declares no limits on changing things there — "Work here as the task requires" is the whole of it.

No component is listed but unattached: the one listed entry resolves to a folder that exists. The opposite case does occur, though — `shop/src/app.js` exists on disk but no `shop` component appears in the registry.

**4. Where is a decision that affects two components at once recorded?**

`PROJECT.md:49`:
> "Project-wide documentation and decisions belong here, in `.docs/` and `.docs/decisions/`."

A cross-component decision is project-wide, so it belongs in `.docs/decisions/`. Note `PROJECT.md:51`: "`.docs/` does not exist yet." — the folder would have to be created.

**5. Which single file is the one to read first, and why?**

`PROJECT.md`. Both entry-point files point at it and nothing else. `CLAUDE.md:3-4` and `AGENTS.md:3-4` carry the same line:
> "Read `PROJECT.md` in this folder before working anywhere in this project. It holds the principles, the agent boundaries and the registry of every component."

And `PROJECT.md:3-5` says of itself: "**AI Project Entry Point** ... Read this before working anywhere in this project."
